(text "One 47k pull-down sits on the isolator input. Lofrans load is 3.3 V / 47k = 70 uA. A second 47k would double that and is not fitted.\\n10 uA leakage in 47k is 0.47 V, below VIL. 100k would be 1.0 V and can cross VIL, so the load cannot be reduced further on this leakage spec.\\n1 nF at the isolator input with the 10k series resistor is about 10 us, still far under the 30 ms debounce, and it replaces the noise margin the lighter DC load gives up.\\nISO7721 (no F suffix) defaults high if the field supply is off. High is idle. The existing firmware counts a rising edge, not a held low.\\nLofrans position is one shunt on pins 1-2. DRY_A stays open, so the pull-up cannot reach REED_ISO, LOFRANS_NODE or REED_SIG.\\nDry position is the same shunt on pins 2-3. LOFRANS_NODE stays open, so the pull-up reaches the isolator and does not reach REED_SIG.\\nDefault assembly is pins 1-2. Fit one shunt only. Two shunts would short pin 1 to pin 3.\\nWith the shunt removed, R23 holds REED_ISO low. A held level is not a pulse.\\nISO7721 without the F suffix holds its output high when VCC2 is below its UVLO and VCC1 is valid, and the output is high-impedance when VCC1 is below UVLO.\\nVCC1 is the same +3V3 as the ESP32, so the MCU is not running while the output side is unpowered.\\nThe existing firmware samples the pin at start and does not treat that sample as an edge. It counts a change only after 30 ms, and only when the new level is high and a direction sense input is already active.\\nField-supply startup and jumper removal produce a falling edge or no edge. A rising edge from supply shutdown or from inserting the shunt is ignored while the windlass sense is stopped.\\nR20 and the clamps stay on the Lofrans node in both positions. JP1 only removes the CAN isolator supply. Do not fit both sources at once.\\nChain length stays the NVS calibration, default 0.36 m per pulse." (at 20 110 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "4188cadc-85f3-4acd-86bb-86b7b40ecb60"))
  (embedded_fonts no)
)
